== When one request improves on every measured cost
For each complete dialogue we tally a newly correct answer, a lost answer, a shared success or a shared failure. A gain satisfies all three cost conditions only when the loop also has strictly lower total wall time, summed first-token time and maximum MLX allocation for that dialogue. The same three comparisons in the opposite direction identify a loss that also cost Base less. In multi-message cases every user request must meet its registered correctness endpoint. DROP questions remain separate here; their paired passage score governs inference in the primary study. Timing is a single observed run per arm.

